---
description: Server-side hardening (validation, JSON-only API routes, Supabase SSR)
globs:
  - src/app/api/**/*.ts
  - src/app/**/actions.ts
  - src/lib/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: true
---

Hardening rules for Server Actions, Route Handlers, and server lib modules.

- Validate inputs before DB calls (zod `safeParse` if available; otherwise explicit guards).
- Route Handlers return JSON only via `NextResponse.json()`. Never return HTML for API paths.
- Use `createClient()` from `@/lib/supabase/server` — never service-role key in code reachable from client bundle.
- Server Actions return structured `{ data }` / `{ error }` for predictable client handling.
- Wrap unexpected errors; do not leak raw Postgres errors to clients.
- After mutations: call `revalidatePath()` / `revalidateTag()` when cached data must refresh.
- Do not import server-only modules into Client Components (check `"use client"` boundary).
- Auth/session: rely on Supabase SSR + middleware; do not reimplement token parsing in actions.
